        "title": "The Evolution of Testing",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Era 1 is backstory — you shipped software in this era. The trajectory matters more than the detail. The constraint was this: humans are slow, inconsistent, and can't scale. Every new feature meant more manual regression coverage. The critical insight that ended the era: if you can describe what correct looks like, a computer can check it 10,000 times per second. That insight is what Era 2 operationalized."
    },
